      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T21:10:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll be honest, I don\u0027t love this behavior. When I invoke a command, I generally want it to do what I ask it, so reordering feels wrong. I could imagine someone potentially specifying a switch twice even, and expecting that switch to get executed twice. Give that all() could be made to have the most desirable default ordering, is there a reason to not allow alternative orderings to be specified?",
